  "summary": "Reviewed all 7 patients on the 'DOAC dose review - week of 10/19/2026' list (grp-doac-review) under RBC-PHARM-07. Each change or correction has a progress note citing its sources.\n\n- pt-0061 Irene Castellano (apixaban): changed from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She finished itraconazole on 8/14 (ID letter). Age 74, 78 kg, SCr 1.02, so no dose criteria are met.\n- pt-0003 Frank Delgado (rivaroxaban): first lowered to 15 mg using the St. Brigid SCr of 160 µmol/L. During the review the lab corrected that result to 118 µmol/L (1.33 mg/dL; the first run had an analyzer calibration fault). CrCl is 59.9, so I set the dose back to 20 mg daily (mr-t0010). Net result: no change from his old dose. Correction note written.\n- pt-0041 Raymond Duquette (apixaban): changed from 5 to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005). No criteria are met, but he has an active itraconazole order.\n- pt-0062 Norman Fairweather (apixaban 5 mg twice daily): no change. St. Brigid ED creatinines came in during the review: 1.70 mg/dL on 10/21, then 1.13 on 10/22. The latest is used, so the only criterion met is age 82. No-change note written.\n- pt-0038 Eugene Moravec (rivaroxaban): changed from 15 to 20 mg daily (mr-t0007). The May 2026 pharmacist screen used ideal body weight, which the policy doesn't allow. With his actual weight (96 kg), CrCl is 56.1. He then sent a portal message with a home-scale weight of 185 lb. A patient-reported weight doesn't count under the policy, so the decision stands. If a clinic weight confirms the loss, CrCl would be about 49 and the dose should be reviewed again.\n- pt-0043 Marjorie Pellegrino (rivaroxaban): changed from 20 to 15 mg daily (mr-t0009). A new SCr of 1.25 (drawn 10/22) came in during the review; with female, age 75 and 71 kg, CrCl is 43.6.\n- pt-0002 Harold Vance (apixaban): first raised from 2.5 to 5 mg twice daily. Since his February kidney injury, weight is back to 64.9 kg and SCr to 1.21, leaving age 82 as the only criterion. Then a St. Brigid dermatology letter arrived saying itraconazole was started 10/22 for 12 weeks, so I set the dose back to 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0015). Correction note written.\n\nFor pt-0041 and pt-0002, the apixaban dose should be reviewed again when the itraconazole courses end; for pt-0002 that is about mid-January 2027. No other medications were changed.\n\nI closed the 5 inbox items that arrived during the review (inbox-a0001 through a0005), each linked to its note or order. No other new items came in. The older inbox items for patients not on this list were left for you.",
